  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_013: scvi_n200, multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat; acc=0.715) has been validated across multiple runs, but the image encoder dimension remains completely unexplored—only imagenet_vit_l has been tested, and its image-only baseline was very weak (0.227). Config_018 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, concat) changes only the image encoder relative to config_013, cleanly isolating the effect of image representation while holding the proven-best RNA encoder, profile setting, aggregation, and fusion fixed. This is the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact design choice left untested: if resnet50 outperforms imagenet_vit_l, it opens a new optimization direction; if it underperforms, it confirms imagenet_vit_l is the right choice and lets us focus remaining budget on other axes (e.g., pca_n2000 or transformer aggregation). Under a limited budget, resolving this binary image-encoder question with a single controlled comparison is more informative than testing a second-order variation (e.g., transformer aggregation) on an already well-characterized axis."
}

